{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"40e082c4dc741dfe387451be4732005fa7682d2efe2fc9798309b6454b0fc11e","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI command interface","key_entities":["rebar bridge fsck","rebar bridge check-access","rebar bridge setup","bridge-fsck","bridge-probe","jira-onboard","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","bridge_fsck.main","_bridge_probe","jira_onboard"],"problem_keywords":["cli verb rename","bridge command","backwards compatibility","consumer migration","argparse dispatch"],"propositions":["Three CLI verbs are renamed to nest under a bridge noun: `bridge-fsck` becomes `bridge fsck`, `bridge-probe` becomes `bridge check-access`, and `jira-onboard` becomes `bridge setup`.","Old verb spellings are retained as functional compatibility entrypoints routing to identical implementations, preserving output schemas, exit codes, options, and behavior.","`bridge setup` calls `bridge check-access` as its final validation step with env overlay and `--no-validate` escape hatch preserved.","`check-access` ships as its own verb rather than a flag because it creates and deletes real Jira issues, unlike read-only flag precedents.","All in-tree consumers including CLI dispatch, help files, schemas, scripts, workflows, and tests are migrated to canonical spellings in a single atomic change."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786701161263486001,"uuid":"b443fc5d-8b5f-4b96-85dc-acd717bce764"}